4600
04:17:19,240 --> 04:17:28,300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: medyo tinatamad na, Mr. President, na pumunta pa sa Clark para makapunta lang sa Coron,

4601
04:17:28,300 --> 04:17:30,620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: dahil nga po dun lumayo.

4602
04:17:31,320 --> 04:17:32,320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So nabawasan po.

4603
04:17:32,480 --> 04:17:34,860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The Department of Tourism noticed this.

4604
04:17:35,220 --> 04:17:40,380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Noong magkaroon po ng paglilipat ng ika nga naka-turbo prop na aeroplano,

4605
04:17:40,780 --> 04:17:46,060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: maliliit na airplanes that they use para po sa mga island na mga destinations natin.

4606
04:17:46,180 --> 04:17:48,580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So people, Mr. President, are tired.

4607
04:17:48,940 --> 04:17:52,920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So instead of going to local destinations, halos pareho lang naman ang presyo,

4608
04:17:52,920 --> 04:17:57,640
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: they'd rather go overseas, they'd rather go to Thailand to go there.

4609
04:17:57,640 --> 04:17:59,740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Or Vietnam, which is more cheaper.

4610
04:18:00,300 --> 04:18:01,560
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So yun po ang nagiging problem.

4611
04:18:01,740 --> 04:18:09,420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kaya nga po, we have already, in one of the hearings, I've already asked the DOTR to look into this.

4612
04:18:09,780 --> 04:18:10,840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Paano pwedeng gawin?

4613
04:18:10,920 --> 04:18:13,020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kasi tinatamad po yung mga kababayan natin.

4614
04:18:13,400 --> 04:18:16,840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Instead of going to Clark, mapapatagal po ang biyahe nila,

4615
04:18:17,360 --> 04:18:19,480
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: e pupunta na lang po sa ibang bansa at mas mura pa.

4616
04:18:19,480 --> 04:18:25,780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Another issue, Mr. President, is yung cost po ng fair ng aeroplano.

4617
04:18:26,220 --> 04:18:27,400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ang sagot po kasi dyan,

4618
04:18:27,640 --> 04:18:29,720
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: mga airline industries,

4619
04:18:30,400 --> 04:18:34,020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: sinasagot na po kasi ng pasahero dahil hindi po napupuno.

4620
04:18:34,460 --> 04:18:38,040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Like if you're going, kaya nga po may mga areas tayo dito sa Pilipinas,

4621
04:18:38,560 --> 04:18:42,280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: like in my Maropa, in my area, in my region,

4622
04:18:42,820 --> 04:18:45,820
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: may mga flights po dati dyan sa Marinduque,

4623
04:18:45,920 --> 04:18:47,900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: may mga flights po dati dyan sa Rumblon,

4624
04:18:48,420 --> 04:18:50,320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: naputol na po because it's so expensive,

4625
04:18:50,320 --> 04:18:52,160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: hindi po napupuno yung flights.

4626
04:18:52,740 --> 04:18:56,560
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Parang pinagbabayad po yung isang pasahero, round trip ka agad.

4627
04:18:56,880 --> 04:18:57,620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So para pagbalik,

4628
04:18:57,680 --> 04:18:59,420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: ng aeroplano, parang may sakay na pasahero.

4629
04:18:59,680 --> 04:19:03,040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So the fees are so exorbitant, masyadong malaki.

4630
04:19:03,040 --> 04:19:11,580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kaya this turns off yung mga would-be local tourists in several local destinations, Mr. President.

4631
04:19:11,620 --> 04:19:17,420
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: So, well, then we expect the department to reason to find solutions

4632
04:19:17,420 --> 04:19:26,180
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: and suggest solutions to the executive department when it comes to these issues, hopefully.

4633
04:19:26,180 --> 04:19:26,280
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Hopefully.

4634
04:19:27,640 --> 04:19:33,680
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Mr. President, actually, there's an ongoing dialogue with the Department of Tourism

4635
04:19:33,680 --> 04:19:36,080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and the Department of Transportation regarding this matter.

4636
04:19:36,600 --> 04:19:41,500
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Pero when it comes po dun sa airline, kailangan din po isama ang NMIC

4637
04:19:41,500 --> 04:19:44,740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: because sila po yung may control, sila po yung may instruction.

4638
04:19:44,920 --> 04:19:51,180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Naalisin na po yung mga turboprop airplanes going to small island tourist destination.

4639
04:19:51,560 --> 04:19:52,980
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Inilipat na po nila sa Clark.

4640
04:19:53,060 --> 04:19:53,940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So that is the problem.

4641
04:19:54,360 --> 04:19:57,580
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: People are getting tired traveling to Clark.

4642
04:19:57,580 --> 04:20:02,960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: For another hour, then when they come home, they have to travel again another hour going back to Metro Manila.

4643
04:20:03,360 --> 04:20:05,660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Kaya po doon nakita na may problema ho dito.

4644
04:20:05,880 --> 04:20:06,320
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ika nga.

4645
04:20:06,820 --> 04:20:11,200
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Because yung travel time, it's so expensive.

4646
04:20:12,360 --> 04:20:16,440
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: But there is a coordination between the DOT and the DOTR.

4647
04:20:16,740 --> 04:20:18,240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Alright. We will look forward to that.

4648
04:20:18,660 --> 04:20:19,220
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you.

4649
04:20:20,120 --> 04:20:21,240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Let me move on.

4650
04:20:21,240 --> 04:20:27,240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: One of the best ways to teach history and share the...

4651
04:20:27,580 --> 04:20:31,980
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: The beautiful culture of the Philippines is through tourism.

4652
04:20:32,740 --> 04:20:39,720
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Would you have any plans to put up more museums and other interactive displays

4653
04:20:39,720 --> 04:20:42,780
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: in our top tourism destinations for this purpose?

4654
04:20:44,720 --> 04:20:49,220
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And would it be included in your budget for 2027?

4655
04:20:57,580 --> 04:21:18,340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: If the president is asking if there's a plan to set up more museums,

4656
04:21:18,340 --> 04:21:24,340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: unfortunately, there is none right now, Mr. President, because of budget constraints.

4657
04:21:24,580 --> 04:21:27,340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Pero what DOT is doing is upgrading training programs.

4658
04:21:27,580 --> 04:21:33,960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: For tour guides, another thing, cultural heritage destinations, pinapalakas po yun.

4659
04:21:34,360 --> 04:21:40,960
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Like in archaeological sites, museums, world heritage, treasuries, cultural properties, etc.

4660
04:21:41,700 --> 04:21:43,920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Then creative tourism, new generation tourism,

4661
04:21:44,000 --> 04:21:49,140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: that places an emphasis on engaging tourists with local culture, arts, and heritage, Mr. President.

4662
04:21:50,160 --> 04:21:55,660
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I hope the department tries to develop the idea.

4663
04:21:55,660 --> 04:21:56,660
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I think it's a very...

4664
04:21:57,580 --> 04:22:04,000
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Well, to include also, Mr. President, we still have the Nayang Pilipino right now.

4665
04:22:04,000 --> 04:22:13,740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Total open space and museum visitors was listed at 11,165 as of October 2026, Mr. President.

4666
04:22:16,020 --> 04:22:16,900
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Okay.

4667
04:22:18,480 --> 04:22:22,020
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Again, I move forward.

4668
04:22:23,200 --> 04:22:26,820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: For the National Parks Development Committee,

4669
04:22:26,820 --> 04:22:34,820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: it's very obvious that there are lesser public parks in the metros for children to play

4670
04:22:34,820 --> 04:22:40,340
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: and for families to just lounge around for free.

4671
04:22:40,840 --> 04:22:44,000
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: In fact, we have more malls than parks.

4672
04:22:45,580 --> 04:22:51,220
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Do we have plans of acquiring lots and creating free parks and conducive open spaces?

4673
04:22:52,020 --> 04:22:55,200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Whether Metro Manila or other parts of the country,

4674
04:22:55,200 --> 04:22:56,200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: because the LGUs may...

4675
04:22:56,820 --> 04:23:01,780
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: may be harnessed to support this move by the department.

4676
04:23:01,780 --> 04:23:11,180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: As much as they would love to focus on developing more parks, Mr. President,

4677
04:23:11,700 --> 04:23:16,540
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: unfortunately, the funding gaps for park development is down to 65 million,

4678
04:23:16,940 --> 04:23:21,780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: or they needed 65 million to complete the Japanese Garden Redevelopment Landscape Utilities.

4679
04:23:22,820 --> 04:23:26,780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: For fiscal year 2027 budget, reductions may affect priority programs,

4680
04:23:26,820 --> 04:23:27,900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and capital outlay.

4681
04:23:28,540 --> 04:23:31,200
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: National Parks Development Committee,

4682
04:23:31,880 --> 04:23:35,260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: in their GAA last year, 2026,

4683
04:23:35,600 --> 04:23:38,000
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: it was like 316.8 million.

4684
04:23:38,640 --> 04:23:41,860
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Pero in the NEP of 2027, it's down to 286.

4685
04:23:42,180 --> 04:23:46,260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Well, we will try, the Senate will try to maintain that at 286.

4686
04:23:46,920 --> 04:23:50,820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And also, can't you try to...

4687
04:23:50,820 --> 04:23:55,240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: can't the department try to coordinate with local government units?

4688
04:23:55,240 --> 04:23:55,300
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Yes.

4689
04:23:56,820 --> 04:23:58,540
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Because the LGUs may have a lot of ideas.

4690
04:23:59,140 --> 04:24:06,420
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Maybe by coordinating with them, helping the tourism department,

4691
04:24:06,860 --> 04:24:07,880
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: maybe there are things like that.

4692
04:24:08,040 --> 04:24:13,040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Just bringing up the idea, Your Honor, Mr. President.

4693
04:24:15,500 --> 04:24:19,060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Unfortunately, according to the DOT, Mr. President,

4694
04:24:19,740 --> 04:24:26,180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: there is no funding yet for such activity or programs.

4695
04:24:26,820 --> 04:24:28,080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: As of yet.

4696
04:24:28,580 --> 04:24:36,920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So, it's very hard for them to look for, to develop parks in different parts of our country.

4697
04:24:38,200 --> 04:24:44,820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Well, as I said, baka pwedeng in coordination with some LGUs na maluluwag pa.

4698
04:24:45,340 --> 04:24:55,200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Anyway, again, I throw the idea to the department for their consideration.

4699
04:24:55,700 --> 04:24:56,500
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: No.

4700
04:24:56,820 --> 04:25:03,300
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I heard you earlier mention figures about international tourists.

4701
04:25:03,880 --> 04:25:09,600
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: In 2015, and this is based on the old records that I have now, so correct me if I'm wrong,

4702
04:25:10,660 --> 04:25:14,040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: we had roughly 5.3 million international tourists.

4703
04:25:14,920 --> 04:25:18,920
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: For reference, Vietnam had around 7.9 million.

4704
04:25:18,920 --> 04:25:26,300
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: So now, in 2025, 10 years after, we have 6.8 million.

4705
04:25:26,440 --> 04:25:26,800
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Is that correct?

4706
04:25:26,820 --> 04:25:34,560
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: But Vietnam has now 21.2 million international tourists.

4707
04:25:35,560 --> 04:25:45,260
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: My question is, why in the past decade, our tourism generally could be said as static?

4708
04:25:47,980 --> 04:25:50,900
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Parang maliit yung itinaas natin.

4709
04:25:51,440 --> 04:25:53,060
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ngunit sila ay napakalaki.

4710
04:25:53,160 --> 04:25:53,940
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ano bang nangyari?

4711
04:25:54,060 --> 04:25:54,820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ano bang diferensya?

4712
04:25:54,820 --> 04:25:55,240
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ano ba?

4713
04:25:56,820 --> 04:25:59,140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Ano mga malaking pag-uulang natin?

4714
04:26:08,780 --> 04:26:10,120
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Alright, Mr. President.

4715
04:26:10,400 --> 04:26:16,380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The explanation of the Department of Tourism, the reason why our country is lagging behind in tourist arrivals,

4716
04:26:16,380 --> 04:26:24,760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: our neighbors, Thailand, Malaysia, and Vietnam, have been investing big amounts for tourism.

4717
04:26:25,460 --> 04:26:26,400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: While tayo po,

4718
04:26:26,400 --> 04:26:28,660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: compared to those countries,

4719
04:26:29,240 --> 04:26:32,760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: is only like about one-fourth of how much they spend.

4720
04:26:34,260 --> 04:26:36,420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: I'll give you some figures, Mr. President.

4721
04:26:36,420 --> 04:26:46,260
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: For example, the budget of Thailand for tourism in 2024 is $167.9 million.

4722
04:26:46,920 --> 04:26:47,660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: This is in dollars.

4723
04:26:48,220 --> 04:26:50,940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Malaysia at $262.87 million.

4724
04:26:51,500 --> 04:26:53,420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Vietnam at $147.92.

4725
04:26:54,520 --> 04:26:56,380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Singapore at $431.2.

4726
04:26:56,400 --> 04:27:00,140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Indonesia at $34.36 million.

4727
04:27:00,760 --> 04:27:03,380
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Philippines is just $52.1 million.

4728
04:27:04,180 --> 04:27:07,020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So, ang arrival po, makikita din, that will translate.

4729
04:27:08,220 --> 04:27:18,280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The Thailand expenditure on the tourism brought them around 35.55 million tourists in 2024.

4730
04:27:18,480 --> 04:27:21,040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Malaysia, $25.02 million.

4731
04:27:21,540 --> 04:27:23,800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Vietnam, $17.58 million.

4732
04:27:24,020 --> 04:27:25,180
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Singapore, $16 million.

4733
04:27:25,180 --> 04:27:26,240
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Indonesia, $17.58 million.

4734
04:27:26,240 --> 04:27:27,740
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Malaysia, $13.89 million.

4735
04:27:28,480 --> 04:27:33,920
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: And because of our funding, we only got 5.95 million tourists, Mr. President.

4736
04:27:36,920 --> 04:27:38,040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: So, poonan.

4737
04:27:38,900 --> 04:27:39,460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Poonan.

4738
04:27:40,100 --> 04:27:43,420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: The problem really, it's a fact, Mr. President.

4739
04:27:43,600 --> 04:27:46,060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So, that's where we're having problems right now.

4740
04:27:46,340 --> 04:27:48,300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Even in advertisements, Mr. President,

4741
04:27:48,640 --> 04:27:52,940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: if you notice other countries like Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand,

4742
04:27:52,940 --> 04:27:55,640
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: you will see them in international news.

4743
04:27:56,240 --> 04:27:58,680
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: CNN, BBC, Fox News.

4744
04:27:59,000 --> 04:28:04,660
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: They advertise major newspapers, New York Times, etc., Singapore's Three Times.

4745
04:28:05,040 --> 04:28:05,520
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: They are there.

4746
04:28:06,180 --> 04:28:10,020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Unfortunately, because of a limited budget, we cannot afford.

4747
04:28:10,560 --> 04:28:13,780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We did that a couple of years ago in the buses of England,

4748
04:28:13,900 --> 04:28:21,980
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: but that's not enough to boost, to advertise our tourism in the Philippines, Mr. President.

4749
04:28:22,900 --> 04:28:26,000
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Well, thank you for your answers.

4750
04:28:26,240 --> 04:28:27,760
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And thank you to the department.

4751
04:28:28,080 --> 04:28:34,980
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: But, well, I hope we could get back to the drawing board.

4752
04:28:36,080 --> 04:28:37,060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Let me add to that.

4753
04:28:37,060 --> 04:28:43,040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And study the possibilities of these suggestions that might be able to develop.

4754
04:28:43,660 --> 04:28:46,900
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Another thing, Mr. President, is like,

4755
04:28:47,580 --> 04:28:53,100
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: I myself would suggest to the DOT to stick with one branding campaign.

4756
04:28:53,100 --> 04:28:56,040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Because we noticed the change of administration.

4757
04:28:56,240 --> 04:29:01,360
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Before, it's like, now it's love the Philippines.

4758
04:29:01,620 --> 04:29:08,020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Before, it was like, wow, Philippines during the time of former Senator Gordon.

4759
04:29:08,540 --> 04:29:13,200
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: And then, it's more fun in the Philippines.

4760
04:29:13,780 --> 04:29:14,780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Wala siyang identity.

4761
04:29:14,980 --> 04:29:16,220
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We don't have an identity.

4762
04:29:16,760 --> 04:29:19,780
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Unlike Malaysia, Mr. President, if you notice in the commercials,

4763
04:29:20,320 --> 04:29:22,840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: they've been using this for the past 20 years.

4764
04:29:23,480 --> 04:29:24,940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Malaysia, truly Asia.

4765
04:29:25,360 --> 04:29:26,160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Tayo,

4766
04:29:26,440 --> 04:29:29,000
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: nakailang palit na ho tayo for the past 20 years.

4767
04:29:29,380 --> 04:29:31,040
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: So, I guess we have to stick to that brand.

4768
04:29:31,160 --> 04:29:32,460
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: para tatatak po sa isipan,

4769
04:29:33,100 --> 04:29:34,080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: magkakaroon ng recall.

4770
04:29:35,820 --> 04:29:37,060
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Philippines should be there.

4771
04:29:37,140 --> 04:29:37,840
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Love the Philippines.

4772
04:29:38,040 --> 04:29:40,020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: And then, let's stick with love the Philippines

4773
04:29:40,020 --> 04:29:43,080
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: so that it will stick to the minds of the viewers and listeners

4774
04:29:43,080 --> 04:29:46,160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: listening to the advertisements of the DOT.

4775
04:29:46,460 --> 04:29:46,880
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Mr. President.

4776
04:29:48,800 --> 04:29:51,920
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Just to end my interpellation, Your Honor,

4777
04:29:52,080 --> 04:29:55,460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I have a suggestion that you should study that.

4778
04:29:55,460 --> 04:29:57,760
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Tutal, meron tayong mga pinag-usapan na ganyan.

4779
04:29:58,180 --> 04:29:59,100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Pero ito, ibang klase.

4780
04:30:00,000 --> 04:30:06,540
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Many years ago, during the younger days of myself and Senator Aimee Marcos,

4781
04:30:07,960 --> 04:30:10,520
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Hawaii was not that popular.

4782
04:30:11,640 --> 04:30:13,140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Diba? It was not that popular.

4783
04:30:13,580 --> 04:30:15,860
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: You know what the Department of Tourism of Hawaii did?

