11810
09:41:10,380 --> 09:41:10,760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you.

11811
09:41:11,000 --> 09:41:15,480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I'll put on record lang din naman na the studies abound now,

11812
09:41:15,580 --> 09:41:16,620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: that it's really dangerous.

11813
09:41:16,780 --> 09:41:18,120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And they call it...

11814
09:41:18,120 --> 09:41:19,120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ano pang iinakamatay?

11815
09:41:20,120 --> 09:41:27,380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: There's this term, uh, concocted called EVALI, yung death by vaping.

11816
09:41:27,640 --> 09:41:28,100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: EVALI?

11817
09:41:28,720 --> 09:41:29,240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: EVALI.

11818
09:41:29,620 --> 09:41:30,140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: EVALI.

11819
09:41:30,220 --> 09:41:31,320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that an acronym, Mr. President?

11820
09:41:31,320 --> 09:41:37,140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yeah, it's an acronym for basically complications that lead to death that result from vaping.

11821
09:41:37,200 --> 09:41:38,140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Anyway, I'll leave it at that.

11822
09:41:38,420 --> 09:41:40,860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Talagang marami pang, mahaba pa yung gabi natin.

11823
09:41:41,220 --> 09:41:46,260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yung second question ko lang naman is about our, um, virology law.

11824
09:41:46,760 --> 09:41:49,260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Alam ni Secretary yan na I wanted assurance

11825
09:41:49,260 --> 09:41:57,320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: that when we roll this out, hindi rin mahahamper ang iba-ibang agencies natin involved in research,

11826
09:41:57,400 --> 09:41:58,960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: including the RITM.

11827
09:41:59,400 --> 09:42:04,660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I, again, again, uh, I will harp on whole of government approach.

11828
09:42:05,080 --> 09:42:06,940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Alam ko, these are independent agencies.

11829
09:42:07,120 --> 09:42:08,940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: RITM is under DOH.

11830
09:42:09,380 --> 09:42:14,560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Um, but I just need that assurance na tulong-tulong tayo to support each other.

11831
09:42:14,560 --> 09:42:19,200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And question ko lang is on the rules na, um, we heard.

11832
09:42:19,260 --> 09:42:21,440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Natapos na, but we didn't see the publication.

11833
09:42:21,760 --> 09:42:22,720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, just a quick update.

11834
09:42:22,880 --> 09:42:24,360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Where are we with virology?

11835
09:42:24,720 --> 09:42:25,760
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Uh, yes, Mr. President.

11836
09:42:26,000 --> 09:42:30,340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Uh, so, DOST is part of the board of RITM and they will, ano?

11837
09:42:32,120 --> 09:42:32,460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ah, sorry.

11838
09:42:33,020 --> 09:42:39,600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: RITM is the part of the board of, of the virology and vaccine institute, no?

11839
09:42:40,060 --> 09:42:45,220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And, um, uh, the update here, Mr. President, is that the IRR has been signed and published.

11840
09:42:45,300 --> 09:42:45,620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

11841
09:42:46,000 --> 09:42:46,680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Uh, published.

11842
09:42:46,800 --> 09:42:47,340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, so.

11843
09:42:47,340 --> 09:42:48,660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The board is composed.

11844
09:42:49,260 --> 09:42:54,100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And that there is now a transition team, uh, to establish its, um, implementation.

11845
09:42:57,240 --> 09:42:59,980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sige, we, we're not aware of, of the publication.

11846
09:43:00,160 --> 09:43:00,980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, can we see na lang?

11847
09:43:01,080 --> 09:43:01,180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi.

11848
09:43:01,420 --> 09:43:03,440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Um, it was published, uh, April.

11849
09:43:03,840 --> 09:43:08,620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, the IRR was signed April 28, 2026 and published May 19.

11850
09:43:10,120 --> 09:43:11,420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ah, no, no, sorry.

11851
09:43:11,500 --> 09:43:13,700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The IRR was signed April 28, 2026.

11852
09:43:13,920 --> 09:43:15,300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The law was published in 2025.

11853
09:43:16,320 --> 09:43:17,380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But the IRR?

11854
09:43:17,380 --> 09:43:18,560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It, uh.

11855
09:43:19,260 --> 09:43:20,500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: May 19.

11856
09:43:20,920 --> 09:43:21,420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ah, sorry.

11857
09:43:21,560 --> 09:43:23,740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It, uh, the IRR was signed.

11858
09:43:24,960 --> 09:43:25,400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: No.

11859
09:43:25,720 --> 09:43:26,160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sorry.

11860
09:43:34,360 --> 09:43:34,500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sorry.

11861
09:43:34,560 --> 09:43:35,200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There's a typo.

11862
09:43:35,600 --> 09:43:37,800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: May typo po yung kanilang kodigo dito.

11863
09:43:37,960 --> 09:43:43,980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, the IRR was signed on April 28, 2026 and published on May 19, 2026.

11864
09:43:44,520 --> 09:43:46,140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And we can provide a copy today.

11865
09:43:46,360 --> 09:43:46,540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We can just get a copy.

11866
09:43:46,680 --> 09:43:47,320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you so much.

11867
09:43:47,380 --> 09:43:47,740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That's all.

11868
09:43:47,800 --> 09:43:48,380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That's all I have.

11869
09:43:48,440 --> 09:43:48,820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you.

11870
09:43:48,980 --> 09:43:49,240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you.

11871
09:43:49,300 --> 09:43:49,820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you, Mr. President.

11872
09:43:49,940 --> 09:43:52,180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, we will be providing you a copy of the IRR.

11873
09:43:52,300 --> 09:43:52,700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you.

11874
09:43:52,960 --> 09:43:54,120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Please, uh, submit na lang.

11875
09:43:55,760 --> 09:44:00,580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Um, may we recognize Senator Marcos for her interjection?

11876
09:44:01,720 --> 09:44:04,000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, uh, the majority floor leader is pointing.

11877
09:44:05,040 --> 09:44:06,800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, go ahead, Senator Marcos.

11878
09:44:07,440 --> 09:44:08,320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay, thank you.

11879
09:44:08,440 --> 09:44:15,040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Uh, Senator Goh also manifested that he wanted to ask, but, uh, since I'm standing here, let's go.

11880
09:44:15,040 --> 09:44:15,860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay.

11881
09:44:16,460 --> 09:44:18,660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Um, the, uh.

11882
09:44:19,260 --> 09:44:30,300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Probably the only encouraging economic number that came out was, uh, the 26% increase in the export of electronics products.

11883
09:44:30,300 --> 09:44:44,520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And following reports of the DOST and the Semiconductor and Electronics Industries of the Philippines are exploring the establishment of a wafer fabrication facility estimated at 10 million U.S. dollars at first.

11884
09:44:45,700 --> 09:44:49,220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Thereafter, rejected by the DOST.

11885
09:44:49,220 --> 09:44:54,940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And now, it is tagged at 30 million dollars.

11886
09:44:55,100 --> 09:44:59,860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What is the precise status of the feasibility study and discussion?

11887
09:45:00,000 --> 09:45:07,940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I'm totally perplexed by this constant postponement of the wafer fabrication facility

11888
09:45:07,940 --> 09:45:11,440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: because it is such a low-lying fruit.

11889
09:45:12,080 --> 09:45:15,840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 62% of our exports is in electronics.

11890
09:45:16,500 --> 09:45:19,220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At hindi man lamang natin matulungan yung electronics.

11891
09:45:20,220 --> 09:45:26,940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Siguro nasa 6 na taon na, na humihingi sila ng wafer fabrication facility.

11892
09:45:26,940 --> 09:45:29,720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nag-umpisa sa 10 million US na reject.

11893
09:45:30,420 --> 09:45:36,220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kaya nagtataka ako, kung gusto natin mag-improve yung trade imbalance,

11894
09:45:36,620 --> 09:45:44,560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: ang unang tutulungan natin itong electronics at naunahan na rin tayo ng Japan, ng Malaysia at ng Thailand.

11895
09:45:45,680 --> 09:45:49,840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Wala ba tayong balak gawan na ng paraan ito?

11896
09:45:49,940 --> 09:45:53,080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 30 million dollars is not the biggest amount in our budget

11897
09:45:53,080 --> 09:45:56,720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and certainly, given the performance,

11898
09:45:56,940 --> 09:45:59,740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: of the electronics industry, they deserve our support.

11899
09:45:59,920 --> 09:46:02,520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, Mr. President, I got an update from the Secretary

11900
09:46:02,520 --> 09:46:07,120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: that US Trade is undergoing the feasibility study.

11901
09:46:08,220 --> 09:46:08,700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: With?

11902
09:46:10,000 --> 09:46:10,600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Naku po!

11903
09:46:11,740 --> 09:46:12,340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: USTDA.

11904
09:46:12,620 --> 09:46:16,240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So USTDA is doing the feasibility study

11905
09:46:16,240 --> 09:46:20,200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: and pending the output of that study,

11906
09:46:20,480 --> 09:46:22,300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: we will know if it will push through or not.

11907
09:46:22,700 --> 09:46:24,440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Whether this project will push through or not.

11908
09:46:24,440 --> 09:46:26,100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Is there a time frame involved?

11909
09:46:26,420 --> 09:46:26,440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Given that...

11910
09:46:27,800 --> 09:46:30,400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We are in intense competition

11911
09:46:30,400 --> 09:46:32,840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and we've already lost our rivals.

11912
09:46:33,800 --> 09:46:34,820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang tagal na nito eh.

11913
09:46:35,600 --> 09:46:37,780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We've been at the assembly level,

11914
09:46:38,240 --> 09:46:40,440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: assembly and kitting level since the 1970s.

11915
09:46:41,260 --> 09:46:43,900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi na tayo nag-move on sa electronics industry.

11916
09:46:44,360 --> 09:46:50,640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dahil ang ating pamahalaan ay hindi nag-i-invest dito nga sa higher level.

11917
09:46:50,900 --> 09:46:52,240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Mag-level up tayo.

11918
09:46:52,240 --> 09:46:56,900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, Mr. President, I've been informed that the feasibility study,

11919
09:46:56,940 --> 09:46:59,020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: will be finished by next year.

11920
09:46:59,640 --> 09:47:01,940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, it is only next year that we will find out

11921
09:47:01,940 --> 09:47:03,780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: whether this project will push through or not.

11922
09:47:03,960 --> 09:47:07,540
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nalulungkot nga ako kasi hindi ko nakikita sa ating budget.

11923
09:47:10,000 --> 09:47:12,200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What's the government's financial commitment?

11924
09:47:12,380 --> 09:47:15,500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Is this going to be charged against the GIA, the Grants in Aid?

11925
09:47:16,160 --> 09:47:16,580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

11926
09:47:17,020 --> 09:47:23,260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And have we begun to identify potential industrial partners and off-takers

11927
09:47:23,260 --> 09:47:26,900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: to guarantee the long term?

11928
09:47:26,940 --> 09:47:30,220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And what's the viability of this entire project?

11929
09:47:31,540 --> 09:47:33,100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Marami kasing bibili niyan, di ba?

11930
09:47:33,220 --> 09:47:35,680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Patok na patok ang AI, data centers.

11931
09:47:35,940 --> 09:47:37,880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The demand is burgeoning.

11932
09:47:38,300 --> 09:47:41,520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And it's really a very, very easy sell.

11933
09:47:43,320 --> 09:47:47,720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, the research itself, the proponent is an academic institution.

11934
09:47:48,800 --> 09:47:52,300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We will know the output of that next year.

11935
09:47:52,300 --> 09:47:56,920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And then, next year, we will determine whether we will push through or not.

11936
09:47:57,460 --> 09:47:59,980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sana maituloy na yan. Napakatagal na yan eh.

11937
09:48:01,540 --> 09:48:04,020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And the funding, sorry, just to complete,

11938
09:48:04,180 --> 09:48:06,720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the funding for the project will be in the Grants in Aid.

11939
09:48:07,320 --> 09:48:07,920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: In the?

11940
09:48:08,380 --> 09:48:09,300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: In the GIA.

11941
09:48:09,920 --> 09:48:10,260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: GIA.

11942
09:48:10,480 --> 09:48:15,020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, the process, Mr. President, is that feasibility studies are ongoing.

11943
09:48:15,340 --> 09:48:16,620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: They'll finish the feasibility study.

11944
09:48:17,100 --> 09:48:18,960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Go or no go based on the feasibility study.

11945
09:48:19,100 --> 09:48:21,080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: If it's a go, it will be charged to the GIA.

11946
09:48:21,080 --> 09:48:26,580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: In terms of marketing, has any firms already committed to using the lab?

11947
09:48:26,740 --> 09:48:26,920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Or should they?

11948
09:48:26,940 --> 09:48:27,840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Or sharing its cost?

11949
09:48:27,960 --> 09:48:28,960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: No, no, Mr. President.

11950
09:48:29,320 --> 09:48:30,160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, I'm a little bit...

11951
09:48:30,160 --> 09:48:32,360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: They're at an earlier stage, which is the feasibility study.

11952
09:48:32,360 --> 09:48:38,840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, but having said that, even in the most important part of the feasibility study is the marketing, certainly.

11953
09:48:40,660 --> 09:48:44,440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sayang lang yung FS kung wala pa kayong mga partners.

11954
09:48:45,020 --> 09:48:51,820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi alam na alam natin sa mga electronics company, marami dyan are willing to share the cost of putting up the lab.

11955
09:48:51,820 --> 09:48:52,820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The company is willing to partner...

11956
09:48:56,940 --> 09:48:59,360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: SEIPI is willing to partner on this project.

11957
09:48:59,640 --> 09:48:59,920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's correct.

11958
09:49:00,040 --> 09:49:08,900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And many of the factories that belong to the Saipi Association are perfectly happy to share cost and guarantee X amount of export.

11959
09:49:09,320 --> 09:49:14,620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, sana magawa ng paraan niyan na bilisan kasi ang tagal-tagal na ninihingi niyan sa totoo lang.

11960
09:49:15,040 --> 09:49:15,780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nakakatawa na.

11961
09:49:16,160 --> 09:49:20,820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The Philippines slipped from 50 to 52.

11962
09:49:21,120 --> 09:49:24,620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Bumagsak pa sa 2026 Global Innovation Index.

11963
09:49:24,620 --> 09:49:26,620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And the DST has acknowledged

11964
09:49:26,940 --> 09:49:33,820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: weaknesses in R&amp;D, the number of STEM students, and the country's researcher base.

11965
09:49:34,420 --> 09:49:41,040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What concrete interventions are very clear in your 2027 budget?

11966
09:49:41,640 --> 09:49:46,280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi parang business as usual lang, samantalang tayo'y nahuhuli.

11967
09:49:46,600 --> 09:49:51,740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We are lagging behind, and yet the budget looks like business as usual.

11968
09:49:56,940 --> 09:50:01,080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, in terms...

11969
09:50:01,080 --> 09:50:03,200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And this is from the Secretary, Mr. President.

11970
09:50:03,720 --> 09:50:13,800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: In terms of the input, admittedly it is low, but they're committed to really increase the output based on the innovations that the agency is doing.

11971
09:50:13,800 --> 09:50:23,320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, it may seem low, and it is low in many respects, but they commit that the output will be worth the decrease that we had,

11972
09:50:23,420 --> 09:50:26,120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: and to arrest any decrease that we've had in the world rankings.

11973
09:50:26,480 --> 09:50:26,820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

11974
09:50:26,940 --> 09:50:28,100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Because it's quite alarming.

11975
09:50:28,720 --> 09:50:32,940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Lahat ng Southeast Asia halos umaakyat dun sa global innovation.

11976
09:50:33,460 --> 09:50:34,260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tayo, pababa.

11977
09:50:34,640 --> 09:50:35,600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nakaka-nervous yun.

11978
09:50:35,600 --> 09:50:42,300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kahit sabihin natin na two places lang yan, yung tangent na pabagsak, e hindi maganda.

11979
09:50:42,800 --> 09:50:53,600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Have we set some targets in terms of number of patent applications, number of technology exports, private sector investment?

11980
09:50:54,500 --> 09:50:56,600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: May targets na ba tayo for research exports?

11981
09:50:56,940 --> 09:50:57,360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Or expenditure?

11982
09:50:57,920 --> 09:51:00,080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi parang pareho lang nun, nakalipas.

11983
09:51:01,900 --> 09:51:04,360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, Mr. President, I've been informed.

11984
09:51:05,580 --> 09:51:08,780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, the ranking is composed of different indicators.

