Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, thank you, Mr. President.

14358
11:44:16,320 --> 11:44:17,060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I wasn't sure

14359
11:44:17,060 --> 11:44:19,160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: if that's the question.

14360
11:44:19,760 --> 11:44:21,300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Maybe I can ask that

14361
11:44:21,300 --> 11:44:21,960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: for a comment

14362
11:44:21,960 --> 11:44:23,240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: from the agency head.

14363
11:44:23,700 --> 11:44:24,860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Are there talks about this

14364
11:44:24,860 --> 11:44:26,220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: being used for warfare?

14365
11:44:26,220 --> 11:44:28,240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Of course, there's none.

14366
11:44:28,400 --> 11:44:29,340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: They said it's commercial.

14367
11:44:30,620 --> 11:44:31,100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There's none.

14368
11:44:31,200 --> 11:44:32,080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, so officially,

14369
11:44:32,240 --> 11:44:33,020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: there's none, Mr. President.

14370
11:44:33,460 --> 11:44:34,720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, thank you very much.

14371
11:44:34,760 --> 11:44:36,440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I just wanted to put that on record

14372
11:44:36,440 --> 11:44:38,400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and hope that

14373
11:44:38,400 --> 11:44:40,440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: as soon as you have more information,

14374
11:44:40,600 --> 11:44:41,640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: you share it with the Senate,

14375
11:44:42,000 --> 11:44:43,340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: which will eventually

14376
11:44:43,340 --> 11:44:45,860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: have to ratify the treaty

14377
11:44:45,860 --> 11:44:47,860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: in the event that there is one.

14378
11:44:47,960 --> 11:44:48,740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Thank you very much.

14379
11:44:48,740 --> 11:44:48,860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's all.

14380
11:44:48,860 --> 11:44:49,580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you, Mr. President.

14381
11:44:49,700 --> 11:44:54,450
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ano ba 'yan? Carabao mango [unclear]. Hindi, okay 'yun, ha.

14382
11:44:54,550 --> 11:44:56,000
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Masarap kaya yun,

14383
11:44:56,220 --> 11:44:58,080
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Senator Imee, Carabao

14384
11:44:58,080 --> 11:44:59,640
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: mango sa space ba ginagawa?

14385
11:44:59,640 --> 11:44:59,940
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes.

14386
11:45:00,000 --> 11:45:14,520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: No, Mr. President. So to clarify, there are a lot of countries who send astronauts. They need space food. And I think it would be cool if our food is found up there. And that can be another economic benefit for the country.

14387
11:45:14,900 --> 11:45:17,280
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pa-try natin sa majority leader natin.

14388
11:45:20,240 --> 11:45:25,780
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I'll eat anything at this point in time, Mr. President. Gutom na ako. Tsaka pagod na rin.

14389
11:45:25,780 --> 11:45:34,220
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Anyway, Mr. President, I move that the budget of the Philippine Space Agency be deemed submitted.

14390
11:45:34,420 --> 11:45:41,880
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Is there any objection? Hearing none, the budget of the Philippine Space Agency is hereby deemed submitted.

14391
11:45:43,380 --> 11:45:48,780
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Next to be taken up, Mr. President, is the budget of the BCDA.

14392
11:45:48,780 --> 11:45:54,780
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: May we recognize the sponsor to give the

14393
11:45:55,780 --> 11:45:57,100
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Summary of the budget of the BCDA.

14394
11:45:57,160 --> 11:46:00,860
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We recognize the sponsor, Senator Bam Aquino.

14395
11:46:02,940 --> 11:46:03,280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Problem.

14396
11:46:14,040 --> 11:46:17,700
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pwede rin natin padalas si majority leader sa outer space.

14397
11:46:20,020 --> 11:46:23,480
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The first majority leader to go to the space.

14398
11:46:23,840 --> 11:46:24,780
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Thank you, thank you.

14399
11:46:34,100 --> 11:46:37,800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: May I be recognized, Mr. President?

14400
11:46:40,040 --> 11:46:43,120
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We recognize the good sponsor, Senator Bam Aquino.

14401
11:46:43,480 --> 11:46:47,380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, Mr. President, thank you for your patience. This is my last agency for today.

14402
11:46:48,440 --> 11:46:54,200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The BCDA, or the Basis Conversion and Development Authority, is up next.

14403
11:46:54,200 --> 11:46:55,200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The subcommittee recommended...

14404
11:46:55,780 --> 11:47:08,020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Retaining 1,147,175,000 national government subsidy proposed under the 2027 General Appropriations Bill.

14405
11:47:08,020 --> 11:47:14,720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: This is the same amount appropriated for BCDA under fiscal year 2026 GAA.

14406
11:47:15,320 --> 11:47:18,820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So wala pong increase from 2026, Mr. President.

14407
11:47:19,240 --> 11:47:24,440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And to note that BCDA actually remits about 14 billion pesos to the National Treasury.

14408
11:47:25,780 --> 11:47:26,780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Every year.

14409
11:47:27,540 --> 11:47:30,360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So with that, Mr. President, we're ready to accept any questions.

14410
11:47:30,860 --> 11:47:35,920
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes, so to interpellate, we recognize...

14411
11:47:35,920 --> 11:47:36,940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ladies first, Mr. President.

14412
11:47:37,080 --> 11:47:38,300
Senate President Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Senator Aimee Marcos.

14413
11:47:45,300 --> 11:47:49,120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ay, oo. Okay. Yes, Mr. Chair, if you could help me here.

14414
11:47:49,120 --> 11:47:56,100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I cannot seem to find any allocation for Pax Silica under the proposed 2027

14415
11:47:56,100 --> 11:48:02,000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: budget of BCDA. Is that correct? There is no allocation for Pax Silica?

14416
11:48:02,000 --> 11:48:03,300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There is none, Mr. President.

14417
11:48:03,300 --> 11:48:10,000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So you categorically confirm that there is no allocation.

14418
11:48:10,440 --> 11:48:19,360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And likewise, there is no allocations for PAC Silica under BCDA's corporate operating budget for 2026 and 2027,

14419
11:48:20,160 --> 11:48:23,020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: including its internally generated funds. Is that correct?

14420
11:48:23,220 --> 11:48:23,720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There is none.

14421
11:48:23,720 --> 11:48:25,220
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So there is no...

14422
11:48:25,220 --> 11:48:29,280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So I'm confirming with our new president, Ariel Nepomuceno.

14423
11:48:29,300 --> 11:48:31,420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, I know him from a past life po.

14424
11:48:31,560 --> 11:48:34,220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Day one, Mr. President, first day.

14425
11:48:34,220 --> 11:48:42,560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So there is no funding for PAC Silica in the GAA or with your internally generated budget.

14426
11:48:42,780 --> 11:48:43,080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, sir.

14427
11:48:43,160 --> 11:48:43,800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So there is none.

14428
11:48:44,340 --> 11:48:54,700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So having confirmed that there is no specific budgetary allocation either in the GAA or the internally generated funds of the BCDA in its corporate operating budget,

14429
11:48:55,220 --> 11:49:03,260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: is there any allocation whatsoever for the compensation and relocation of residents who stand to be displaced by the project?

14430
11:49:03,500 --> 11:49:04,920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, Mr. President.

14431
11:49:06,000 --> 11:49:07,360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Let me confer with them.

14432
11:49:09,060 --> 11:49:12,940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: By the way, Mr. President, in the previous hearing we had about PAC Silica,

14433
11:49:13,500 --> 11:49:20,660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I mentioned to them that it is this representation's position that nothing should be built, nothing should be done

14434
11:49:20,660 --> 11:49:24,660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: if the families, farmers, and IPs in the area are not...

14435
11:49:25,220 --> 11:49:26,520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: provided support,

14436
11:49:27,480 --> 11:49:29,640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: makausap ng maayos,

14437
11:49:30,240 --> 11:49:34,960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: at makakuha ng buy-in dito po sa pinaplano ng gobyerno.

14438
11:49:35,520 --> 11:49:42,880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So I am also interested to find out, Mr. President, if there is a budget for the families that are currently there.

14439
11:49:42,960 --> 11:49:46,000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And since the second hearing has not been scheduled,

14440
11:49:46,000 --> 11:49:54,000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I'm taking this opportunity to find out since notices of eviction apparently are requests for quit claims and waivers.

14441
11:49:55,220 --> 11:50:00,740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Of those residing or owning land in the area have been issued.

14442
11:50:01,920 --> 11:50:04,160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Meron na daw notice eh of eviction.

14443
11:50:04,640 --> 11:50:06,420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Meron na daw quit claim and waiver.

14444
11:50:06,600 --> 11:50:08,280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kinausap na daw yung mga kapitan.

14445
11:50:08,800 --> 11:50:15,720
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kaya gusto namin malaman, kung wala naman sa budget, ano ibibigay doon sa mga paaalisin?

14446
11:50:25,220 --> 11:50:30,400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So how much for next year?

14447
11:50:34,640 --> 11:50:35,560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: P322 million.

14448
11:50:35,820 --> 11:50:36,620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: In the [unclear].

14449
11:50:37,480 --> 11:50:38,000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: In the [unclear].

14450
11:50:38,760 --> 11:50:39,640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ah, sorry, in the...

14451
11:50:39,640 --> 11:50:40,920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay.

14452
11:50:40,920 --> 11:50:46,000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So there is P322 million allocated for financial assistance.

14453
11:50:46,460 --> 11:50:50,160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: This is not particularly in the areas affected by Paxilica.

14454
11:50:50,280 --> 11:50:53,220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: This is in all BCDA areas.

14455
11:50:54,040 --> 11:50:54,920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But if...

14456
11:50:55,220 --> 11:50:58,940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: If ever there would be assistance to the families there, it would be coming from this budget.

14457
11:50:59,040 --> 11:51:00,780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It is not in the ComReport.

14458
11:51:00,900 --> 11:51:02,560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It is in their corporate funds.

14459
11:51:02,880 --> 11:51:05,160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And it's P320 million, is that correct?

14460
11:51:05,820 --> 11:51:07,480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: P322 million, Mr. President.

14461
11:51:07,480 --> 11:51:08,440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: P322 million.

14462
11:51:09,000 --> 11:51:19,500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And have you conducted a comprehensive inventory of the families, farmers, IPs, and other documents directly or indirectly to be displaced by the proposed economic zone?

14463
11:51:19,640 --> 11:51:20,340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, Mr. President.

14464
11:51:20,340 --> 11:51:21,080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: They have, Mr. President.

14465
11:51:21,080 --> 11:51:22,500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And how many will be affected?

14466
11:51:30,720 --> 11:51:31,140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ilan?

14467
11:51:35,460 --> 11:51:36,020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Families.

14468
11:51:36,860 --> 11:51:40,340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi may binigay na mga numero nung meeting natin, 'di ba, Chair?

14469
11:51:40,680 --> 11:51:44,080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Meron silang binibigay na numbers, pero to be continued daw yung pagbibilang.

14470
11:51:46,740 --> 11:51:48,100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ah, Mr. President, so...

14471
11:51:48,100 --> 11:51:48,620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ayun pa rin.

14472
11:51:48,880 --> 11:51:49,360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yun pa rin.

14473
11:51:49,580 --> 11:51:50,120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Walang bago.

14474
11:51:50,220 --> 11:51:53,700
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I know, because during the hearing, nagbigay sila ng numero.

14475
11:51:53,700 --> 11:51:55,200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Lumiit nga, Mr. President, eh.

14476
11:51:55,220 --> 11:51:55,420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Lumiit.

14477
11:51:55,900 --> 11:51:56,260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Eh,

14478
11:51:56,460 --> 11:51:59,280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ngayon, 198 officially from BCDA.

14479
11:51:59,480 --> 11:52:02,220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But if you remember, in our hearing, it was closer to...

14480
11:52:02,820 --> 11:52:03,380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 400.

14481
11:52:03,980 --> 11:52:04,380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 400?

14482
11:52:04,920 --> 11:52:05,140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Right?

14483
11:52:05,540 --> 11:52:09,900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And honestly, Mr. President, latest reports have it higher to about 1,000.

14484
11:52:10,120 --> 11:52:10,500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Correct.

14485
11:52:10,780 --> 11:52:23,260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, it would be good, Mr. President, if maybe an independent agency like DSWD or NCIP could help us with identifying who are the possible families who will be affected.

14486
11:52:23,260 --> 11:52:24,800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Because we want to make sure that...

14487
11:52:24,800 --> 11:52:32,180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We want to make sure that if this initiative does push through, wala pong kababayan na masasagasaan o mapeperwisyo.

14488
11:52:32,180 --> 11:52:42,980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I'm sure you've heard, as well as Senator Padilla and myself, from the IPs, as well as the residents, those in Tarlac and elsewhere,

14489
11:52:43,520 --> 11:52:52,500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: who are very, very concerned because they've really received notices to vacate and the request to sign quit claims and waivers.

14490
11:52:52,500 --> 11:52:53,500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Has BCDA...

14491
11:52:54,800 --> 11:53:04,520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Determined the total amount necessary to compensate these people who will be affected in the loss of their homes, their agricultural land, their livelihood, their crops?

14492
11:53:06,480 --> 11:53:09,200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Meron na kayong estimate kung magkano ang kakailanganin?

14493
11:53:09,340 --> 11:53:10,280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Meron na ba kayong estimate?

14494
11:53:10,340 --> 11:53:12,120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kung kaya ng 322 ninyo?

14495
11:53:12,660 --> 11:53:13,800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, wala pang...

14496
11:53:14,740 --> 11:53:17,060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, has anybody been given quit claims or anything?

14497
11:53:18,160 --> 11:53:24,160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. President, for the record, BCDA is saying that they're still currently talking...

14498
11:53:24,800 --> 11:53:30,200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: To the affected individuals in our hearing, and this is, of course, before Mr. Nepomuceno's time.

14499
11:53:30,740 --> 11:53:39,260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We also enjoined the President then not to do press releases without informing the local leaders first.

14500
11:53:39,380 --> 11:53:43,640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Because even the mayor of Capas found out about this initiative on the news.

14501
11:53:43,640 --> 11:53:44,320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Secario, yes.

14502
11:53:44,320 --> 11:53:47,040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, not even... Nobody really talked to him.

14503
11:53:47,720 --> 11:53:51,680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But, Mr. President, for the record, wala naman daw pong pinapapirmang quit claim.

14504
11:53:51,680 --> 11:53:52,640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, they are denying.

14505
11:53:53,240 --> 11:53:53,400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

14506
11:53:53,440 --> 11:53:54,680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And it would be good if...

14507
11:53:54,800 --> 11:54:02,800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: If we can have another hearing and we have evidence to this that any quick claims were provided to any of the families there.

14508
11:54:03,220 --> 11:54:07,660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Are there any identified potential relocation sites for the affected families?

14509
11:54:10,520 --> 11:54:12,040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, possibly.

14510
11:54:12,700 --> 11:54:13,160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Possibly.

14511
11:54:13,160 --> 11:54:20,100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But, Mr. President, may I also remind everyone that this area is three times the size of BGC.

14512
11:54:20,360 --> 11:54:20,980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's right.

14513
11:54:21,060 --> 11:54:24,740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, whether these are 300, 500, or 1,000 families...

14514
11:54:24,800 --> 11:54:25,800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's right.

14515
11:54:25,800 --> 11:54:33,480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Surely, there needs to be buy-in, there needs to be consent, and there needs to be a good area for them, no?

14516
11:54:33,780 --> 11:54:35,500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Or even to carve out their area.

14517
11:54:35,500 --> 11:54:36,900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Because the area is so huge.

14518
11:54:37,220 --> 11:54:46,200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: You need to derive informed consent, there's cost to develop these areas, to provide them with adequate housing, basic utilities, livelihood opportunities, and so on.

14519
11:54:47,620 --> 11:54:48,620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Mr. President, may I add?

14520
11:54:48,620 --> 11:54:54,020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I also don't know how you can compensate the burial grounds and the ancestors of some of our [unclear].

14521
11:54:54,020 --> 11:54:54,620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mr. President...

14522
11:54:54,800 --> 11:54:56,320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That was brought up in the hearing.

14523
11:54:56,440 --> 11:54:59,500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I suggested we have a burial ground in the middle of this area.

